# Skillet Peanut Butter Chocolate Chip Blondies

Based on [Chrissy Teigen Cravings](https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/252973/cravings-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20251202235345/https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/books/252973/cravings-by-chrissy-teigen-with-adeena-sussman/)), pg. 243

{ rating="2" image="skillet_peanut_butter_chocolate_chip_blondies.jpeg" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] 1 stick [butter]{ ing="butter" }, slightly softened
- [ ] 2/3 cup [crunchy peanut butter]{ ing="crunchy-peanut-butter" }
- [ ] 3/4 [light brown sugar]{ ing="light-brown-sugar" }, packed
- [ ] 2/3 cup [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" }
- [ ] 2 tsp [vanilla extract]{ ing="vanilla-extract" }
- [ ] 2 [eggs]{ ing="egg" }
- [ ] 1.25 cups [flour]{ ing="flour" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [salt]{ ing="salt" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }
- [ ] 2/3 cup [peanut butter]{ ing="peanut-butter" } (or chocolate) chips
- [ ] 2/3 cup [chocolate chips]{ ing="chocolate-chips" } (semi-sweet or dark)

## Recipe

1. Preheat oven to 350 and [butter]{ ing="peanut-butter" } a 10 inch iron skillet
1. With a wooden spoon, beat together the [butter]{ ing="butter" }, peanut butter, [brown sugar]{ ing="light-brown-sugar" }, and [granulated sugar]{ ing="granulated-sugar" } until creamy
1. Add the vanilla, then beat in one [egg]{ ing="egg" } at a time
1. In a small bowl, whisk together the [flour]{ ing="flour" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, and [baking powder]{ ing="baking-powder" }
1. Add the flour mixture to the main mix, then mix in the peanut butter and [chocolate chips]{ ing="chocolate-chips" }
1. Spread the batter into the skillet and bake for 40-45 (when the center is soft and gooey, but outside is golden brown)

## Notes

1. It would be nice to make these less oily and greasy
1. Sometimes you can find bags of peanut butter and chocolate chips, which gives you 2/3 cup leftover for snacking
